Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: isolate Brick FEL recovery from payload rollback

The sunxi board code publishes fel_booted before main_loop(), but the generic
autoboot path still increments the filesystem bootcount and can select the
rollback command.  A volatile recovery boot must try the current payload and
must not change persistent rollback state.  Limit the exception to the Brick
diagnostic configuration; ordinary SD boots keep the existing behavior.

diff --git a/common/autoboot.c b/common/autoboot.c
index 5d356f8..04dbe01 100644
--- a/common/autoboot.c
+++ b/common/autoboot.c
@@ -452,9 +452,13 @@ static void process_fdt_options(void)
 const char *bootdelay_process(void)
 {
 	char *s;
+	bool brick_fel_recovery;
 	int bootdelay;
 
-	bootcount_inc();
+	brick_fel_recovery = IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TRIMUI_BRICK_SD_DIAGNOSTIC) &&
+			     env_get("fel_booted");
+	if (!brick_fel_recovery)
+		bootcount_inc();
 
 	s = env_get("bootdelay");
 	bootdelay = s ? (int)simple_strtol(s, NULL, 10) : CONFIG_BOOTDELAY;
@@ -477,7 +481,7 @@ const char *bootdelay_process(void)
 		s = env_get("failbootcmd");
 	} else
 #endif /* CONFIG_POST */
-	if (bootcount_error())
+	if (!brick_fel_recovery && bootcount_error())
 		s = env_get("altbootcmd");
 	else
 		s = env_get("bootcmd");
